[{:db/id 17592186124443 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-51a75799-7672-5c71-a422-88f2c2c1de7a" "question-bace43f6-9821-5763-9bf8-9ca1cf7da037"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124444 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3edc7251-4f74-5afa-bcee-22e839f081a7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124445 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d13fce5d-8bd4-547a-afec-720ff5befaa7" "question-c3503a39-2405-5c8f-9ad7-2d39b5c187d5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124249 :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}((y-4)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2)) \\\\  & =\\frac{y-4}{x-2} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}((y-4)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y) = \\dfrac {y-4}{x-2} \\, \\mathbf i + \\ln(x-2) \\, \\mathbf j.\n$$\n\nNow, we solve $\\nabla f(x,y) = \\mathbf 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {y-4}{x-2} \\, \\mathbf i + \\ln(x-2) \\, \\mathbf j = 0 \\  \\mathbf i + 0\\ \\mathbf j\n$$\n\nBy equating the coefficients of $\\mathbf{i}$ on both sides of the equation (and similarly with $\\mathbf{j}$), we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y-4}{x-2}=0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2)=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get $y-4=0,$ which means $y=4.$  From the second equation, we obtain $\\ln(x-2)=0,$ which means that $x=3.$\n\nTherefore, $\\nabla f(x,y) =\\mathbf  0$ at the point $(3,4).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124447 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5961ee6e-358e-5baa-837e-dbd941cc54b6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-51a75799-7672-5c71-a422-88f2c2c1de7a" :question/id #uuid "51a75799-7672-5c71-a422-88f2c2c1de7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-127652" :question/problem "Evaluate $∇f(x,y)$ at $(e,1)$ if $f(x,y)={x}^{y}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{y}) \\\\  & =y{x}^{y-1} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{y}) \\\\  & ={x}^{y}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =y{x}^{y-1}\\text{ }i+{x}^{y}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\text{ }j, \\\\ ∇f(e,1) & =1(e)^{1-1}\\,i+{e}^{1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡e\\,j \\\\  & =i+e\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-51d09cbe-76cd-5f94-9148-15ee4e3c70f5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-51d09cbe-76cd-5f94-9148-15ee4e3c70f5" :answer-field/id #uuid "51d09cbe-76cd-5f94-9148-15ee4e3c70f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-15a96f20-3d44-594c-b78c-5063ef876b55" :answer-field/choices ["answer-586b4ce1-ff41-581f-8671-763767e3f3aa" "answer-f50ec89d-eacd-5a88-8f97-5ca1603aa25f" "answer-e58c9d0d-900d-5547-a140-989e42e2459e" "answer-fbc7838c-e6a9-592d-8e12-48498680e92d" "answer-15a96f20-3d44-594c-b78c-5063ef876b55"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-586b4ce1-ff41-581f-8671-763767e3f3aa" :answer/id #uuid "586b4ce1-ff41-581f-8671-763767e3f3aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f50ec89d-eacd-5a88-8f97-5ca1603aa25f" :answer/id #uuid "f50ec89d-eacd-5a88-8f97-5ca1603aa25f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e\\,i+e\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e58c9d0d-900d-5547-a140-989e42e2459e" :answer/id #uuid "e58c9d0d-900d-5547-a140-989e42e2459e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fbc7838c-e6a9-592d-8e12-48498680e92d" :answer/id #uuid "fbc7838c-e6a9-592d-8e12-48498680e92d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "i" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15a96f20-3d44-594c-b78c-5063ef876b55" :answer/id #uuid "15a96f20-3d44-594c-b78c-5063ef876b55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "i+e\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bace43f6-9821-5763-9bf8-9ca1cf7da037" :question/id #uuid "bace43f6-9821-5763-9bf8-9ca1cf7da037" :question/math-academy-id "q-71353" :question/problem "Evaluate $∇h(x,y)$ at $(1,-1)$ if $h(x,y)={e}^{{x}^{2}+xy}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{{x}^{2}+xy}) \\\\  & =(2x+y){e}^{{x}^{2}+xy} \\\\ {h}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{{x}^{2}+xy}) \\\\  & =x{e}^{{x}^{2}+xy}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the gradient is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇h(x,y) & =⟨{h}_{x}(x,y),\\,{h}_{y}(x,y)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(2x+y){e}^{{x}^{2}+xy},\\,x{e}^{{x}^{2}+xy}⟩ \\\\ ∇h(1,-1) & =⟨(2(1)+(-1)){e}^{{1}^{2}+(1)(-1)},\\,1\\cdot {e}^{{1}^{2}+(1)(-1)}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-798ed032-e7e1-5b90-a986-cd5c9792165f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-798ed032-e7e1-5b90-a986-cd5c9792165f" :answer-field/id #uuid "798ed032-e7e1-5b90-a986-cd5c9792165f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b75c28ff-2fd2-5cb7-a89b-d7658bb7354e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-04308c81-1719-5c33-8d40-ebccd5767820" "answer-8e9a1c99-2d0e-5085-aa56-1bc7935a41a6" "answer-b75c28ff-2fd2-5cb7-a89b-d7658bb7354e" "answer-e717d850-f7b3-516d-8057-a5abe63141f9" "answer-d8f83b16-7c14-555d-b3bd-510c637f070d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-04308c81-1719-5c33-8d40-ebccd5767820" :answer/id #uuid "04308c81-1719-5c33-8d40-ebccd5767820" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e9a1c99-2d0e-5085-aa56-1bc7935a41a6" :answer/id #uuid "8e9a1c99-2d0e-5085-aa56-1bc7935a41a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨1,\\,-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b75c28ff-2fd2-5cb7-a89b-d7658bb7354e" :answer/id #uuid "b75c28ff-2fd2-5cb7-a89b-d7658bb7354e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨1,\\,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e717d850-f7b3-516d-8057-a5abe63141f9" :answer/id #uuid "e717d850-f7b3-516d-8057-a5abe63141f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨3,\\,-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d8f83b16-7c14-555d-b3bd-510c637f070d" :answer/id #uuid "d8f83b16-7c14-555d-b3bd-510c637f070d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨3,\\,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3edc7251-4f74-5afa-bcee-22e839f081a7" :question/id #uuid "3edc7251-4f74-5afa-bcee-22e839f081a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-127946" :question/problem "Evaluate $∇h(x,y,z)$ at $(1,-2,2)$ if $h(x,y,z)={x}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{y}^{2}+2yz.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{y}^{2}+2yz) \\\\  & =2x{z}^{2}-{y}^{2} \\\\ {h}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{y}^{2}+2yz) \\\\  & =2z-2xy \\\\ {h}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{y}^{2}+2yz) \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}z+2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇h(x,y,z) & =⟨{h}_{x}(x,y,z),\\,{h}_{y}(x,y,z),\\,{h}_{z}(x,y,z)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2x{z}^{2}-{y}^{2},\\,2z-2xy,\\,2{x}^{2}z+2y⟩ \\\\ ∇h(1,-2,2) & =⟨2(1)(2)^{2}-(-2)^{2},\\,-2(1)(-2)+2(2),\\,2(1)^{2}(2)+2(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8-4,4+4,4-4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,8,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fe5a3950-f690-5d04-879c-231b6f838613"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fe5a3950-f690-5d04-879c-231b6f838613" :answer-field/id #uuid "fe5a3950-f690-5d04-879c-231b6f838613" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bd9e8470-5c37-54ae-b712-f0a64e63b2e2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5b7ebbbc-7508-52dc-91d2-56b705b7eccc" "answer-e7d9044c-103d-5c75-a1cc-b44786993ed3" "answer-763a0475-ce2e-53a8-aa2d-9466219586f6" "answer-c0ae3e99-1ea5-5fa4-a1e9-7139e200dfcc" "answer-bd9e8470-5c37-54ae-b712-f0a64e63b2e2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b7ebbbc-7508-52dc-91d2-56b705b7eccc" :answer/id #uuid "5b7ebbbc-7508-52dc-91d2-56b705b7eccc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-12,0,8⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e7d9044c-103d-5c75-a1cc-b44786993ed3" :answer/id #uuid "e7d9044c-103d-5c75-a1cc-b44786993ed3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-4,0,8⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-763a0475-ce2e-53a8-aa2d-9466219586f6" :answer/id #uuid "763a0475-ce2e-53a8-aa2d-9466219586f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨12,8,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c0ae3e99-1ea5-5fa4-a1e9-7139e200dfcc" :answer/id #uuid "c0ae3e99-1ea5-5fa4-a1e9-7139e200dfcc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨4,-4,8⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd9e8470-5c37-54ae-b712-f0a64e63b2e2" :answer/id #uuid "bd9e8470-5c37-54ae-b712-f0a64e63b2e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨4,8,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d13fce5d-8bd4-547a-afec-720ff5befaa7" :question/id #uuid "d13fce5d-8bd4-547a-afec-720ff5befaa7" :question/math-academy-id "q-71470" :question/problem "Given $h(x,y,z)=xy{e}^{x}+{z}^{2}{e}^{z}.$ Find the points $(x,y,z)$ where $∇h(x,y,z)=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy{e}^{x}+{z}^{2}{e}^{z}) \\\\  & =xy{e}^{x}+y{e}^{x}+0 \\\\  & =y(x+1){e}^{x} \\\\ {h}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy{e}^{x}+{z}^{2}{e}^{z}) \\\\  & =x{e}^{x}+0 \\\\  & =x{e}^{x} \\\\ {h}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy{e}^{x}+{z}^{2}{e}^{z}) \\\\  & =0+2z{e}^{z}+{z}^{2}{e}^{z} \\\\  & =z(2+z){e}^{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇h(x,y,z)=y(x+1){e}^{x}\\,i+x{e}^{x}\\,j+z(2+z){e}^{z}\\,k.$\n\nNow, we solve $∇f(x,y,z)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x+1){e}^{x}\\,i+x{e}^{x}\\,j+z(2+z){e}^{z}\\,k & =0\\text{ }i+0\\text{ }j+0\\text{ }j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by equating the coefficients of $i$, $j$, and $k$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y(x+1){e}^{x}=0 \\\\ x{e}^{x}=0 \\\\ z(2+z){e}^{z}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second equation gives $x=0.$ Substituting these into the first equation, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0+1){e}^{0} & =0 \\\\ y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, from the third equation, we get  $z=0$ or $z=-2.$\n\nTherefore, $∇h(x,y,z)=0$ at two points: $(0,0,0)$ and $(0,0,-2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e83f4999-419d-51c4-a803-c6789f4e1b52"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e83f4999-419d-51c4-a803-c6789f4e1b52" :answer-field/id #uuid "e83f4999-419d-51c4-a803-c6789f4e1b52" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a6cf6f0f-1cc3-5518-a4d7-359da9629347" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6e2a514c-da70-5cc8-95d2-327d72d03570" "answer-fb87d0bd-b556-514b-84e7-e694a530dff2" "answer-a6cf6f0f-1cc3-5518-a4d7-359da9629347" "answer-8f042e63-ea21-547d-8187-c6464d907f1c" "answer-7067d8af-1731-5b47-8f38-e961d32014a4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e2a514c-da70-5cc8-95d2-327d72d03570" :answer/id #uuid "6e2a514c-da70-5cc8-95d2-327d72d03570" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,0,-2)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb87d0bd-b556-514b-84e7-e694a530dff2" :answer/id #uuid "fb87d0bd-b556-514b-84e7-e694a530dff2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,0,0)$ and $(-1,0,-2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6cf6f0f-1cc3-5518-a4d7-359da9629347" :answer/id #uuid "a6cf6f0f-1cc3-5518-a4d7-359da9629347" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,0,0)$ and $(0,0,-2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f042e63-ea21-547d-8187-c6464d907f1c" :answer/id #uuid "8f042e63-ea21-547d-8187-c6464d907f1c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,0,0)$ and $(0,0,2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7067d8af-1731-5b47-8f38-e961d32014a4" :answer/id #uuid "7067d8af-1731-5b47-8f38-e961d32014a4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,0,0)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c3503a39-2405-5c8f-9ad7-2d39b5c187d5" :question/id #uuid "c3503a39-2405-5c8f-9ad7-2d39b5c187d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-128513" :question/problem "Given $h(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+4yz-2{z}^{2}-2{y}^{2}x.$ Find the points $(x,y,z)$ where $∇h(x,y,z)=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+4yz-2{z}^{2}-2{y}^{2}x) \\\\  & =2x-2{y}^{2} \\\\ {h}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+4yz-2{z}^{2}-2{y}^{2}x) \\\\  & =4z-4yx \\\\ {h}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}+4yz-2{z}^{2}-2{y}^{2}x) \\\\  & =4y-4z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇h(x,y,z)=2(x-{y}^{2})\\,i+4(z-yx)\\,j+4(y-z)\\,k.$\n\nNow, we solve $∇f(x,y,z)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x-{y}^{2})\\,i+4(z-yx)\\,j+4(y-z)\\,k & =0\\text{ }i+0\\text{ }j+0\\text{ }j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by equating the coefficients of $i$, $j$, and $k$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-{y}^{2}=0, \\\\ z-yx=0, \\\\ y-z=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first equation gives $x={y}^{2}.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we obtain $z={y}^{3}.$ Substituting $z={y}^{3}$ into the third equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}^{3} & =0 \\\\ y(1-{y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ y & =0,\\,\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y=-1,$ we get $x=(-1)^{2}=1$ and $z=(-1)^{3}=-1.$\n\n- For $y=0,$ we obtain $x={0}^{2}=0$ and $z={0}^{3}=0.$\n\n- For $y=1,$ gives $x={1}^{2}=1$ and $z={1}^{3}=1.$\n\nFinally, $∇h(x,y,z)=0$ at three points: $(1,-1,-1),$ $(0,0,0)$ and $(1,1,1).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e9f85d81-d1f0-5077-ba52-dc9b36b72fa3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e9f85d81-d1f0-5077-ba52-dc9b36b72fa3" :answer-field/id #uuid "e9f85d81-d1f0-5077-ba52-dc9b36b72fa3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3eb3ce4f-3615-5638-9cca-7d5f9a7f4065" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ca48ce3d-8118-5a85-8d40-9f54dccebe39" "answer-2e36d0b8-dad3-53f0-905d-1b73b0cfb007" "answer-b421e42f-f55a-5ffe-a533-367af3998505" "answer-4a50ec3f-8ef4-53d6-b614-888ffb598364" "answer-3eb3ce4f-3615-5638-9cca-7d5f9a7f4065"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca48ce3d-8118-5a85-8d40-9f54dccebe39" :answer/id #uuid "ca48ce3d-8118-5a85-8d40-9f54dccebe39" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-1,-1,-1)$ and $(0,0,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e36d0b8-dad3-53f0-905d-1b73b0cfb007" :answer/id #uuid "2e36d0b8-dad3-53f0-905d-1b73b0cfb007" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-1,-1,-1),$ $(0,0,0)$ and $(1,1,1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b421e42f-f55a-5ffe-a533-367af3998505" :answer/id #uuid "b421e42f-f55a-5ffe-a533-367af3998505" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,-1,-1)$ and $(-1,-1,1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a50ec3f-8ef4-53d6-b614-888ffb598364" :answer/id #uuid "4a50ec3f-8ef4-53d6-b614-888ffb598364" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,-1,-1)$ and $(1,1,1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3eb3ce4f-3615-5638-9cca-7d5f9a7f4065" :answer/id #uuid "3eb3ce4f-3615-5638-9cca-7d5f9a7f4065" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,-1,-1),$ $(0,0,0)$ and $(1,1,1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5961ee6e-358e-5baa-837e-dbd941cc54b6" :question/id #uuid "5961ee6e-358e-5baa-837e-dbd941cc54b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-71515" :question/problem "What is the gradient of the product $f(x,y)h(x,y)$ if $f(x,y)=x{e}^{y}$ and $h(x,y)=y{e}^{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the product of two functions $f(x,y)$ and $h(x,y)$ is given by:\n\n$$\n∇[fh]=f\\,∇\\,h+h\\,∇\\,f\\,\\,\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the partial derivatives of $f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{e}^{y})={e}^{y} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{e}^{y})=x{e}^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\text{ }j={e}^{y}\\text{ }i+x{e}^{y}\\text{ }j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the partial derivatives of $h(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y{e}^{x})=y{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{∂h}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{x})={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇h(x,y) & =\\frac{∂h}{∂x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂h}{∂y}\\text{ }j=y{e}^{x}\\text{ }i+{e}^{x}\\text{ }j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the product rule, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇[f(x,y)h(x,y)] & =x{e}^{y}(y{e}^{x}\\text{ }i+{e}^{x}\\text{ }j)+y{e}^{x}({e}^{y}\\text{ }i+x{e}^{y}\\text{ }j) \\\\  & =xy{e}^{x+y}\\text{ }i+x{e}^{x+y}\\text{ }j+y{e}^{x+y}\\text{ }i+xy{e}^{x+y}\\text{ }j \\\\  & =(x+1)y{e}^{x+y}\\text{ }i+x(1+y){e}^{x+y}\\text{ }j\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-90c23b7b-1640-5aaa-b8b3-64340afb293e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-90c23b7b-1640-5aaa-b8b3-64340afb293e" :answer-field/id #uuid "90c23b7b-1640-5aaa-b8b3-64340afb293e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f072c200-9d5e-5ac5-b478-4233e499425f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f072c200-9d5e-5ac5-b478-4233e499425f" "answer-df8dc6a7-9339-5e43-b61c-4513120ec263" "answer-caf56146-05fe-53cc-92f2-a535ba4943df" "answer-d2acb1a7-39df-54ef-82c2-34bde846d73e" "answer-f9e6b982-9c47-56e1-8b69-4a1e0179c1d1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f072c200-9d5e-5ac5-b478-4233e499425f" :answer/id #uuid "f072c200-9d5e-5ac5-b478-4233e499425f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+1)y{e}^{x+y}\\text{ }i+x(1+y){e}^{x+y}\\text{ }j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df8dc6a7-9339-5e43-b61c-4513120ec263" :answer/id #uuid "df8dc6a7-9339-5e43-b61c-4513120ec263" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+1)y{e}^{x}\\text{ }i+x(1+y){e}^{y}\\text{ }j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-caf56146-05fe-53cc-92f2-a535ba4943df" :answer/id #uuid "caf56146-05fe-53cc-92f2-a535ba4943df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+y)y{e}^{xy}\\text{ }i+x(x+y){e}^{xy}\\text{ }j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2acb1a7-39df-54ef-82c2-34bde846d73e" :answer/id #uuid "d2acb1a7-39df-54ef-82c2-34bde846d73e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+y){e}^{x+y}\\text{ }i+(x+y){e}^{x+y}\\text{ }j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f9e6b982-9c47-56e1-8b69-4a1e0179c1d1" :answer/id #uuid "f9e6b982-9c47-56e1-8b69-4a1e0179c1d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "xy{e}^{xy}\\text{ }i+(x+1)(1+y){e}^{xy}\\text{ }j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186125727 :tutorial/content "For a function of three variables $f(x,y,z)$, the gradient of $f$ is given by the vector  \n\n \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\nabla \\! f (x,y,z) &= f_x(x,y,z)\\ \\mathbf i + f_y (x,y,z)\\ \\mathbf j + f_z (x,y,z)\\ \\mathbf k.\n                             \n}\n$$\n\n \n\nFor a function $f(x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n)$ of $n$ variables, its gradient is usually given as a column vector:\n\n![](images/21/21e05d85506da576e293bce86b1ca98f4f5b101c49b0591a49d80d2a4b8bfcc1.svg)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124727 :activity/expected-seconds 1140.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
